\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Whole-space Wick ordering and the half-Dirichlet state}
\date{2026-11-09}

\p{On #{H_\infty=\ell^2(\epsilon\mathbb Z^2,\epsilon^2;\mathbb R)},
let #{Q_{\epsilon,\infty}=m_0^2\bbI -\covsq_\epsilon} be the positive
operator represented by the whole-lattice incidence form. For the
evaluation functional #{\delta_0:u\mapsto u(0)}, write
#{\delta_0^\sharp} for its Riesz vector. The
\newvocab{whole-space Wick variance} is
##{c_\epsilon(m_0)
 =\delta_0\bigl(Q_{\epsilon,\infty}^{-1}\delta_0^\sharp\bigr).}
Translation covariance makes the same variance apply at every site.}

\p{For #{\phi\in H_{\ell,N}}, multiplication by the real function
#{\phi} is a self-adjoint endomorphism #{M_\phi} of the finite function
algebra. Put #{p_c(u)=u^4-6cu^2+3c^2}. The
\newvocab{whole-space Wick quartic} is the function
##{V_\epsilon(\phi)=\frac{\epsilon^2}{24}
                     \trace p_{c_\epsilon(m_0)}(M_\phi).}
For #{\lambda>0}, the \newvocab{half-Dirichlet law} and its state are
##{\begin{aligned}
Z_{\ell,N}&=\int \ue^{-\lambda V_\epsilon}\,\extd\mu_{Q_{\epsilon,D}},\\
\extd\nu_{\ell,N}&=Z_{\ell,N}^{-1}\ue^{-\lambda V_\epsilon}
                                      \extd\mu_{Q_{\epsilon,D}},\\
\omega_{\ell,N}(F)&=\int F\,\extd\nu_{\ell,N}.
\end{aligned}}
The last map is a \vocabk{complex algebraic state}{fdip-0024}
on bounded measurable observables, with complex conjugation as involution.
Its polynomial extension and positivity of the normalizer follow in
\ref{fdip-00HZ}. It is a
\vocabk{weighted Gaussian law}{fdip-00GH} with the
\vocabk{square Dirichlet form}{fdip-00HU} as precision data.}

\p{These choices are exactly
\citet{(IV.9), (IV.36)-(IV.37), pp. 193, 204-205}{guerra1975euclideanII}.
The Wick variance comes from the whole lattice; the Gaussian measure
comes from the killed form. The distinction is part of the law.}
